    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "Invisalign vs Braces: Choosing the Right Option for Your Smile"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Home Blog 13th Aug, 2025",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "https://drdantegonzales.com/index.php",
          "text": "Home"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://drdantegonzales.com/blog.php",
          "text": "Blog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Ever looked in the mirror and wondered, “Should I go for braces or Invisalign?” Whether you're a teen, young adult, or a working professional, straightening your teeth is a big decision. You want to smile with confidence, but you also want comfort, flexibility, and results. With so many orthodontic treatment options available, choosing the right one can be confusing."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This blog clears the fog around the Invisalign vs braces debate. We’ll break down everything, what they are, how they work, pros and cons, comfort, cost factors, and what suits your lifestyle best. Let’s get straight to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "What Is Invisalign?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Invisalign is a modern orthodontic treatment that uses clear aligners to align teeth into the desired position. These invisible aligners are made from smooth plastic and are custom-designed to fit snugly over your teeth."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Unlike traditional braces, Invisalign doesn’t use metal brackets and wires. Instead, it uses a series of trays that gradually shift your teeth. You wear each set for about two weeks and then switch to the next. They're removable, so you can eat, brush, and floss with ease. Most people won’t even notice you're wearing them. That’s why many patients, especially in social or professional settings, prefer them."
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "../assets/blog/shared/orthodontic-illustration-01.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "What Are Traditional Braces?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Traditional braces are what we usually think of when it comes to braces treatment. They involve metal brackets attached to each tooth, connected by wires and sometimes rubber bands. They apply gentle pressure to slowly shift the teeth into the correct position. Now, they’re not just silver or shiny."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can choose ceramic braces, lingual braces (attached behind the teeth), or even coloured ones. They’re suitable for almost all cases, especially complex orthodontic cases like severe crowding, severely crooked teeth, or major bite issues. While they’re more visible, they’re highly effective and time-tested."
    },
